# vocab/shapes/query-declaration-shapes.ttl
#
# The declaration membrane (R135; extended to every tracked .ttl 2026-08-29, spec §4.6): an
# authored artifact may only name a term one of the owned vocabularies declares.
#
# TWO ARTIFACT FAMILIES, ONE RULE. An etkl:QueryArtifact is read for EVERY owned IRI the query
# mentions (tests/query_terms.py, PROCEDURAL). An etkl:VocabularyArtifact is read for the owned
# IRIs its triples USE AS VOCABULARY, and for the owned subjects of an alignment module
# (vocab/queries/vocabulary-role.rq and alignment-subject.rq, AXIOM / derivation / open world).
# The two derivations emit the SAME predicate deliberately: the demand being made is the same
# demand. SEAM 4 (spec §4.7) was decided by writing this shape BOTH ways and running it — with a
# separate etkl:alignmentSubject predicate the message reads "…tab-fno-align.ttl ALIGNS
# …tab#aggFnSum" instead of "names", while the file and the term are named identically, and a
# second constraint would have to restate this namespace filter and this FILTER NOT EXISTS. One
# invariant, one derivation of it: etkl:alignmentSubject was NOT added.
#
# NEUROSYMBOLIC GATE (CLAUDE.md §8) — AXIOM, CONSTRAINT FORM, CLOSED WORLD. This file
# VALIDATES what the PROCEDURAL extractor (tests/query_terms.py) asserted; it never derives.
# The `FILTER NOT EXISTS` is licensed because it is HOLON-SCOPED: the data graph handed to it
# is exactly the union of the non-align owned ontologies — the vocabulary holon — so "no
# triple has this term as a subject" is a closed question inside that holon, not an inference
# from the absence of evidence in an open world. Do NOT build an "undeclared terms" graph from
# this: deriving `?term a etkl:UndeclaredTerm` from an absence is exactly what §8 forbids.
#
# © 2026 François Rosselet · CC-BY-4.0
@prefix sh:   <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .
@prefix etkl: <https://w3id.org/iladub/etkl#> .

etkl:QueryArtifactShape a sh:NodeShape ;
    sh:targetClass etkl:QueryArtifact ;
    sh:sparql [
        a sh:SPARQLConstraint ;
        sh:message "{$this} names {?term}, which no owned ontology declares" ;
        # SCOPE. The producers emit EVERY owned IRI their artifact names and decide nothing;
        # the choice of which of them must be declared is made HERE, visibly and with a date,
        # rather than invisibly in Python.
        #
        # THE NAMESPACE EXEMPTION IS DELETED (2026-08-29). Until now this filter named five
        # owned namespaces one by one, which excluded `prog:`, `docgov:` and `corpus:` by
        # omission — the three that had no ontology file at all, so that including them would
        # have painted the instrument red on day one for a reason that was not a leak. Those
        # three are now declared in vocab/internal/ and the filter is the SINGLE OWNED ROOT.
        # The deletion IS the oracle: while the exemption existed this instrument could not
        # see those namespaces even if a term went missing from them.
        #
        # This is a NAMESPACE prefix, not a term list — no term is ever typed here (G3). It
        # stays STRSTARTS rather than VALUES because SHACL forbids VALUES inside an sh:sparql
        # constraint, MEASURED 2026-08-28 (R135 F3):
        #     Validation Failure - A SPARQL Constraint must not contain a VALUES clause.
        sh:select """
            SELECT $this ?term WHERE {
                $this <https://w3id.org/iladub/etkl#namesTerm> ?term .
                FILTER ( STRSTARTS(STR(?term), "https://w3id.org/iladub") )
                FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?term ?p ?o }
            }""" ;
    ] .

# The same constraint, over the .ttl family. Its LOGIC is identical by construction — the two
# shapes differ only in sh:targetClass — because the demand is one demand and a second
# derivation of it would be the restatement CLAUDE.md plan-rule 6 forbids.
etkl:VocabularyArtifactShape a sh:NodeShape ;
    sh:targetClass etkl:VocabularyArtifact ;
    sh:sparql [
        a sh:SPARQLConstraint ;
        sh:message "{$this} names {?term}, which no owned vocabulary declares" ;
        sh:select """
            SELECT $this ?term WHERE {
                $this <https://w3id.org/iladub/etkl#namesTerm> ?term .
                FILTER ( STRSTARTS(STR(?term), "https://w3id.org/iladub") )
                FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?term ?p ?o }
            }""" ;
    ] .
